<section xml:id="sec-activecode" label="sec-activecode" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>ActiveCode</title>

  <p>A standard activecode using the normal Runestone js bundle:</p>

  <exercise xml:id="exercise-activecode-baseline" label="activecode-baseline">
    <title>Standard ActiveCode</title>
    <statement>
      <p>Fix the code so that <c>add(a, b)</c> correctly adds two numbers.</p>
    </statement>
    <program xml:id="activecode-baseline" interactive="activecode" language="python">
      <code>
      def add(a,b):
          return 4
      </code>
      <tests>
      from unittest.gui import TestCaseGui

      class myTests(TestCaseGui):

         def testOne(self):
             self.assertEqual(add(2,2), 4, "Adding two identical integers")
             self.assertEqual(add(7,13), 20, "Adding two different integers")
             self.assertAlmostEqual(add(2.0,3.0), 5.0, 5, "Adding two decimal numbers")

      myTests().main()
      </tests>
    </program>
  </exercise>

  <p>A modified activecode that runs in an iframe using a custom Runestone bundle. It displays a message from the Duck API on each run:</p>

  <exercise xml:id="exercise-activecode-experiment" label="activecode-experiment">
    <title>ActiveCode experiment</title>
    <statement>
      <p>Fix the same <c>add(a, b)</c> function in the experimental ActiveCode. The unit tests score your solution.</p>
      <interactive xml:id="interactive-activecode-experiment" platform="javascript" custom-runestone="yes" dark-mode-enabled="yes" design-width="1000" aspect="4:1" source="experiments/activecode.js">
        <slate xml:id="activecode-experiment" surface="html" aspect="3:2">
          <xi:include href="experiments/activecode.xhtml" />
        </slate>
      </interactive>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
</section>
